---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="install">

          <p>
            Vector is free. Create a free Vector account, then download the installer that matches your
            computer, open it, and move through the operating system's installation flow. Vector is available for Apple silicon and Intel Macs, Windows,
            and Linux.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Start with the right build.</strong>
            <span>The download page detects your platform and keeps every architecture available.</span>
            <a class="callout-link" href="/login?returnTo=%2Faccount">Create a free account to download →</a>
          </div>
          <p>
            Every installer, for every architecture, is on <a href="/download">vectordev.ai/download</a> once you
            sign in with your free Vector account. Once installed, Vector updates itself: choose Check now in
            Settings → Updates &amp; about, or Check for Updates in the Vector menu on macOS.
          </p>
          <p>
            New to Vector? <a href="/docs/first-launch">First launch, step by step</a> walks through the download, the
            first-launch warnings, signing in, picking a model and a first task.
          </p>
          <p>
            The terminal agent installs separately. See <a href="/docs/terminal-agent#install-the-cli">Install the CLI</a>.
            If macOS, Windows or Linux refuses to open a preview build, see
            <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
